# Architecture: Repository Layer

- Repositories must handle only persistence logic: read data, save data, update data, delete data, and query data.
- Repository interfaces must live in `app/modules/<module>/domain/repositories.py`.
- SQLAlchemy repository implementations must live in `app/modules/<module>/infrastructure/sqlalchemy_repositories.py`.
- Repositories must encapsulate ORM and database access.
- Repository interfaces must end with `Repository`.
- Repository implementations must include their implementation type in the class name.
- Repository methods must remain storage-focused and explicit about filters, ordering, limits, locking, and write behavior.
- Do not generate JWTs, hash passwords, send emails, call external integrations, localize messages, manage workflows, or coordinate scenarios in repositories.
- Do not enforce business rules unrelated to persistence in repositories.
- Do not automatically commit transactions unless the use case explicitly requires it. Transaction boundaries belong to the use case layer.
